Chapter: RocPolyCaptureId
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_polymorphism_tests.zig, the
 two "captures (polymorphic)" cases:

     ((|id| (|x| id(x)))(|y| y))(41)       41
     ((|id| (|x| id(x)))(|y| y))("ok")     "ok"

 The identity is passed in as a value and captured by a closure that applies
 it. Each line is its own instantiation, Integer and Text, so a front end
 that pins the captured `id` to the first use it sees still has to get the
 second right on its own.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (((\id -> (\x -> id x)) (\y -> y)) 41))
   print-line-uni (((\id -> (\x -> id x)) (\y -> y)) "ok")
  end
